{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5ee465c4-253d-49dd-a442-13aa5dad8ecb",
    "name": "task-router API",
    "description": "Requests for the task-router IVR routing engine (Spring Boot, com.rusk.routing).\n\nSelect the **task-router local** environment, start the app, then run the folders in order with the Collection Runner. Requests save the IDs they create into collection variables, so later requests reuse them.\n\nThe routing scenarios assume the sample rules from src/main/resources/db/seed.sql:\n- Spanish line +18005550199 -> spanish\n- Billing line +18005550100 -> billing\n- Tech line +18005550111 from a +1512 caller -> tech-support\n- Anything else -> general (catch-all)\n\nThe DTMF folder also needs one menu rule: pressing 1 on the billing line goes to payments. Its description has the SQL to create it.\n\nEvery create request needs a callId, the telephony platform's call ID. It is the idempotency key: repeating a request with the same callId returns the original interaction with 200 instead of creating a new one. The optional dtmfInput field holds the digits the caller pressed in the IVR menu.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. IVR routing (create and route)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create and route a call",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('callId', 'call-' + Date.now());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Routed to tech-support', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('ROUTED');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.routedQueue.name).to.eql('tech-support');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.matchedRule.name).to.eql('Tech line, Austin area');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Location header points to the interaction', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Location')).to.include('/api/interactions/' + body.id);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('interactionId', body.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "id": "5eeab2bb-d60c-429e-a8a3-2fc9ae5ec057",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"callId\": \"{{callId}}\",\n  \"callerNumber\": \"+15125550000\",\n  \"dialedNumber\": \"+18005550111\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/interactions/route",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "interactions",
                "route"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Retry with the same call ID",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK, not a new interaction', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Same interaction and decision as the first request', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(String(body.id)).to.eql(String(pm.collectionVariables.get('interactionId')));",
                  "    pm.expect(body.routedQueue.name).to.eql('tech-support');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
